UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 1366(d), S corporation losses are deductible only to the extent of the shareholder''s stock and debt basis. Losses first reduce stock basis to zero ($10,000 absorbed), then the remaining $10,000 reduces debt basis from $15,000 to $5,000, yielding stock $0 and debt $5,000.
Wrong (B): This reverses the required ordering. Stock basis must be reduced to zero before any loss reduces debt basis under Section 1367(a)(2).
Wrong (C): This ignores the debt basis reduction entirely. The remaining $10,000 loss after exhausting stock basis must reduce debt basis.
