-- Q1006: Advanced Basis Calculations [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 1367(b)(2)(B) and Treas. Reg. Section 1.1367-2(c), when an S corporation shareholder''s losses have reduced both stock and debt basis, subsequent income restores debt basis first up to its original amount before increasing stock basis. This reverse ordering ensures the shareholder''s loan is made whole before stock basis increases.
Wrong (B): This states the restoration follows the same order as loss absorption. The restoration order is the reverse of the loss deduction sequence under Section 1367(b)(2)(A).
Wrong (C): There is no pro rata restoration mechanism. The Code requires sequential restoration—debt first, then stock.
Wrong (D): Both stock and debt basis are restored by subsequent income, not just stock basis.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1006;

-- Q1007: Advanced Basis Calculations [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Section 722 and Section 752, initial outside basis equals cash contributed ($50,000) minus the liability assumed by the partnership ($30,000), plus the partner''s 40% share of that partnership liability ($12,000). The calculation is $50,000 − $30,000 + $12,000 = $32,000.
Wrong (A): $50,000 ignores the liability adjustment entirely. Section 752(b) treats the partnership''s assumption of the partner''s liability as a deemed distribution reducing basis.
Wrong (C): $80,000 incorrectly adds the full liability to the cash contribution instead of netting the deemed distribution against the deemed contribution.
Wrong (D): $20,000 subtracts the full $30,000 liability without adding back the partner''s 40% allocable share under Section 752(a).$EXPL$
