-- Q1016: Trusts and Estates [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 665, the throwback rules for accumulation distributions were largely repealed for domestic trusts by the Tax Reform Act of 1997. Accumulated income distributed in Year 2 is taxed to beneficiaries as ordinary income under Section 662 without throwback treatment. The trust receives a distribution deduction under Section 661 for the amount distributed.
Wrong (A): Throwback treatment taxing beneficiaries as if income were distributed in Year 1 no longer applies to domestic trusts after the 1997 repeal.
Wrong (B): Double taxation in both years does not occur. The trust is taxed in Year 1 on retained income, and the beneficiary is taxed in Year 2 on the distribution, but the trust receives a deduction in Year 2.
Wrong (D): The distribution is not tax-exempt. Beneficiaries include the distribution in income under Section 662.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1016;

