-- Q1019: Trusts and Estates [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 661(a), a trust''s distribution deduction equals the lesser of DNI under Section 643(a) or the amount actually distributed to beneficiaries. Since $120,000 distributed is less than $185,000 DNI, the deduction is $120,000. The trust pays tax on the remaining $65,000 of undistributed income.
Wrong (A): $200,000 is gross income before trustee fees, not the distribution deduction. The deduction cannot exceed actual distributions.
Wrong (B): $185,000 is the DNI amount but the trust only distributed $120,000. The deduction is capped at amounts actually paid or required to be distributed.
Wrong (D): $65,000 is the undistributed taxable income remaining after the deduction, not the deduction itself.$EXPL$
