-- Q1021: Trusts and Estates [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under IRC Sec. 664(b) and Treas. Reg. Sec. 1.664-1(d)(1), charitable remainder trust distributions use a four-tier ordering system: (1) ordinary income, (2) capital gains, (3) other tax-exempt income, and (4) corpus. The $60,000 distribution exhausts all three income tiers ($40,000 + $15,000 + $5,000) before reaching corpus.
Wrong (A): Characterizing the entire $60,000 as ordinary income ignores the four-tier system. Capital gains and tax-exempt income must be separately identified.
Wrong (C): Treating $20,000 as return of corpus is incorrect because the trust has $60,000 of total income across all tiers, fully covering the distribution.
Wrong (D): Characterizing $60,000 as capital gain violates the worst-in-first-out ordering. Ordinary income in tier 1 must be exhausted before capital gains in tier 2.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1021;

